# Line endings are deterministic here regardless of anyone's core.autocrlf.
#
# This repo is Windows-first but its tooling is run through bash/sh, so the two
# families must not be normalised the same way:
#
#   - install.ps1 is CRLF with a UTF-8 BOM and must stay that way. It is the
#     single source of truth and carries every embedded script as a here-string;
#     a silent LF conversion turns a three-line change into a whole-file diff.
#   - The shell scripts must be LF. A .sh checked out with CRLF fails as
#     `bash: \r: command not found`, which reads as a broken tool, not a broken
#     checkout.
#
* text=auto

install.ps1     text eol=crlf

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
